=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is operating correctly in both directions. Full end-to-end bidirectional connectivity between pc1 (195.11.14.2) and pc2 (200.1.1.2) was confirmed by live ping tests: pc1→pc2 returned 4/4 replies (0% loss, ~0.96 ms RTT) and pc2→pc1 returned 4/4 replies (0% loss, ~1.20 ms RTT).

The control plane is equally clean. Router1 (AS 1) and router2 (AS 2) have established an eBGP session over the 193.10.11.0/24 transit link. Router1 correctly advertises 195.11.14.0/24 (pc1's LAN) and has learned 200.1.1.0/24 via BGP from router2. Router2 correctly advertises 200.1.1.0/24 (pc2's LAN) and has learned 195.11.14.0/24 via BGP from router1. Both prefixes are installed in each router's FIB as best BGP routes. No route-maps, prefix-lists, or access-lists are applied anywhere in either router's configuration, so there is no policy that could selectively block return traffic. Both end-hosts have appropriate default gateways pointing to their local router.

The user's perception that "replies never come back" does not correspond to any measurable fault in the network infrastructure. The symptom is a false premise — the return path through router2→router1→pc1 is intact and forwarding correctly. No corrective action is required on the network side; the issue, if real, should be investigated at the application or host level on the user's machine.
=== END ===